                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b47b9145-1c06-306f-9e0d-b626989ae9ca",
                        "entry_id": "9b802b3d-6cd7-33a3-9e94-e4e323ed683d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An aversion to autocratic leadership; a policy of limiting the power of leaders."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a5329980-a9a5-4d8a-b617-f223fa3780d9",
                                "sense_id": "b47b9145-1c06-306f-9e0d-b626989ae9ca",
                                "text": "Although tyrannophilia (D. Pikes) had not yet set in, the traditional tyrannophobia (Thomas Hobbes) had been partially set out of joint."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "841af1aa-4674-4596-acff-dd079d345021",
                                "sense_id": "b47b9145-1c06-306f-9e0d-b626989ae9ca",
                                "text": "On the other hand, if tyrannophobia hampers useful grants of power to the executive, it creates social costs, namely and entrenched reluctance to transfer necessary powers to the executive."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0047f8a-b466-48cd-bd17-c27845e79039",
                                "sense_id": "b47b9145-1c06-306f-9e0d-b626989ae9ca",
                                "text": "Indeed, if the aim is to minimize the risk of dictatorship, or just to take optimal precautions against it, tyrannophobia might be counterproductive, for reasons we will discuss."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
